====================================================================================================
CAMPAIGN-V3 DOE
====================================================================================================
CAVEAT: each arm's val_transmission_at_selection is read at that arm's OWN selection optimum -- selection metrics differ by arm by design. The response itself is the uniformly-computed validation transmission loss, compared at each run's own best epoch; that is the designed comparison, not a confound.
NO RATE, SLOPE, OR THRESHOLD METRIC APPEARS ANYWHERE IN THIS ANALYSIS. Every length response is a full-curve Huber loss at a fixed length.

Decision (2026-08-26): sub_t (substitution response) REMOVED from the tested/printed response set -- r=+0.95 with in-distribution transmission fit across the 32 v3 Hamiltonian cells, cannot be separated from fitting. Old reports carrying a stray 'sub_t' key are read tolerantly (not an abort); the value is simply not analyzed. (decision 1, 2026-08-26: r=+0.95 with in-distribution fit, not separable from fitting)

CI RESPONSE ADDED: ['ci_interior_mode'] (ham-only, decision 2, 2026-08-26). ham BH family size is now 15 terms x 7 responses = 105 (dropped sub_t, added ci_interior_mode). ['ci_interior_total'] is merged and exported but DESCRIPTIVE ONLY, no F-test (2026-09-01: it is the mode axis plus two small components in quadrature -- a near-copy of the headline that would only pad the family). Companion columns (['onsite_abs_mean', 'onsite_std', 'val_transmission_at_selection', 'l16_transmission']) are printed beside their best/worst cells.

